>
	<p>
		I'm Amin Khani, a Software Engineer who works across two closely related disciplines:
		<strong>Django backend development</strong> and <strong>security engineering</strong>. I like
		building backend systems that are not just functional, but hardened, monitored, and resilient
		against real-world threats.
	</p>

	<h2>What I do</h2>
	<p>
		I design and build secure backend services with Django and Django REST Framework — APIs,
		real-time systems with Django Channels, background processing with Celery, and geospatial
		features with GeoDjango. On the security side, I work on OS hardening, patch and
		vulnerability management, malware analysis, and SOC-style threat detection and incident
		response.
	</p>
	<p>
		I'm currently a <strong>Security Solutions Deployment Engineer</strong> at
		<a href="https://aps-co.net/" target="_blank">Andisheh Pardazan e Sepahan (APS-Co)</a>, where I
		deploy and configure enterprise security platforms — including Kaspersky Next EDR Expert and
		XDR Expert — across client environments running Docker and Kubernetes. I work directly with
		client IT and security teams to integrate new tooling into existing infrastructure across
		Linux, Windows, and containerized environments, and I help configure SOC workflows for threat
		detection, malware, and incident analysis.
	</p>
	<p>
		Before that, I spent nearly two years as a <strong>Software Engineer</strong> at
		<a href="https://fardaadco.ir/" target="_blank">Fardaad Co.</a>, designing and developing secure
		backend services with Django and DRF. I implemented patch management workflows to reduce
		exposure to known vulnerabilities, conducted vulnerability assessments using CVE and NVD
		databases, applied CIS benchmark hardening policies, and built an SSH firewall handler that
		significantly cut down unauthorized access attempts. I also worked closely with DevOps
		pipelines to keep security monitoring continuous.
	</p>

	<h2>Open source</h2>
	<p>
		I maintain <a href="https://github.com/aminkhani/secap" target="_blank">SECAP</a>, a
		cross-platform automated system hardening framework for auditing and enforcing security
		baselines on Windows and Linux, aligned with CIS Benchmarks and DISA STIG standards. It
		automates detection of misconfigurations and remediation of insecure defaults on both
		operating systems.
	</p>

	<h2>Education</h2>
	<p>
		I hold a Bachelor's degree in Computer Engineering from the
		<strong>University of Kashan</strong> (2021–2024), graduating with a 16/20. My undergraduate
		project focused on sentiment analysis using a semi-supervised GAN, and I ranked 1st in a
		master's-level Reinforcement Learning elective.
	</p>

